{
  "Columns": "",
  "The value’s key (a dotted path reads a nested value) and the header text (`Bind<string>`).": "",
  "`text`, `number`, `date`, `boolean`, `list`: alignment, format, sorting and the editor (`TextBox`, `NumberBox`, `DateBox`, `CheckBox`, `DropDown`).": "",
  "Pixels (default: the `columnWidth` and `columnMinWidth` settings); `flex` shares the free space until the user resizes.": "",
  "Pinned to an edge (a column in a band sticks with its band); hidden at first; the alignment.": "",
  "The band a column given flat sits in (its `name` or place); its place in the order columns hide in to fit the width, the lowest first.": "",
  "Read the value another way; show it another way — `Intl` options for a number or date column (`{ style: 'currency', currency: 'EUR' }`, which an Excel export turns into the number format too) or a function that writes the text; sort it another way (rows in memory).": "",
  "`(ctx) => component`: content of your own, made once per pooled cell; read `ctx.row` and `ctx.value` in getters.": "",
  "`(ctx) => Field | component`: an editor of your own. A `Field` is read through its value; anything else calls `ctx.setValue`.": "",
  "An empty value is not taken; `(value, row, context) => message`; the choices of a list (an array, or a function `(row, context)`, also async). `row` is the row itself; `context.values` holds what was entered, `context.getValue(field)` the entered value else the row’s.": "",
  "the standard grid’s rule set (`required`, `numeric`, `range`, `stringLength`, `pattern`, `email`, `compare`, `custom`, `async`), checked after `required` and `validate`. See [Validation rules](/datagrid/forms#rules).": "",
  "The column in the edit form: `visible`, `colSpan`, `label`, `helpText`, `editorOptions`, `order`.": "",
  "The conditions the filter row offers for the column, and the one it starts with.": "",
  "`Bind<number | number[] | 'year' | 'quarter' | 'month' | 'day' | 'hour' | 'minute' | 'second' | null>`: how the header filter groups the values. A number column in ranges of that size (“0 – 100”; several sizes make a tree), a date column in a tree of its parts down to that one (default: the `headerFilterDateInterval` setting, `day`); `null` lists every value. A range picked filters with `>=` its start and `<` its end. See [Ranges, dates and entries](/datagrid/filtering#intervals).": "",
  "`{ text, value, count? }[]` or `(request) => items`: the header filter’s entries instead of the values; a value may be a filter expression. The function gets `{ column, filter, signal, values() }` — `values()` gives the values it would list.": "",
  "`Bind<unknown[]>`, `Bind<'include' | 'exclude'>`: the values chosen in the header filter, and whether they keep the rows or leave them out. A function is followed; `grid.filters` holds them as `values` and `filterType`.": "",
  "`GridLookup`: the cell keeps a key and shows the text of its item from another source (see [Lookup columns](/datagrid/lookups#lookups)). `type` still decides the alignment.": "",
  "The text of a lookup cell read from the row (`'customer.name'` or `(row) => text`): the source is then asked only to edit and to list. The field a server sorts the column by.": "",
  "`(values, value, row, context) => void | Promise`: called when the user commits a value (editor, paste, Delete), before it is written. `values` starts as `{ [field]: value }`; add fields to write them too. `row` is the row itself, `context` the values entered so far (`values`, `getValue(field)`). A promise keeps the cell busy until it settles.": "",
  "Switch a feature for this column; wins over `settings`.": "",
  "How this column’s edge is dragged (`widget` or `nextColumn`); wins over `settings`.": "",
  "`standard`: the column keeps its cells out of view; `virtual`: it gets them only in view (see [Virtual columns](/datagrid/scrolling#virtual-columns)); wins over `settings`.": "",
  "`(ctx) => component | Node | string`: content of your own in the header in place of the title text, made once; `ctx.title`, `ctx.sort`, `ctx.column` in getters. The title stays the header’s accessible name.": "",
  "How the user opens this column’s editor; wins over `settings`.": "",
  "A yes/no column: the pasted texts read as yes and as no; wins over `settings`.": "",
  "`Bind<number | undefined>`: the column’s place among the grouped columns; the rows start grouped by it. A function is followed: a new value moves the column there, `undefined` ungroups it.": "",
  "The column’s groups start open; wins over `autoExpandAll`.": "",
  "The grouping switches for this column; each wins over `settings`.": "",
  "`(a, b) => number`: the order of the column’s groups in memory (`dir` still turns it).": "",
  "`(row) => value` for rows in memory, or the field a server groups by: what the rows are grouped and the groups ordered by instead of the value.": "",
  "`(ctx) => component`: content of your own in the column’s group rows, made once per pooled group row; read `ctx.value`, `ctx.text`, `ctx.count`, `ctx.level`, `ctx.key`, `ctx.isExpanded`, `ctx.summaryItems` (`{ name, column, summaryType, value, text }` of the group row) in getters.": "",
  "Move between cells, the headers included. In a right-to-left page Left and Right swap.": "",
  "The first data column / the last column; the first / the last row (only that block is loaded; infinite: the last row shown, and the next part loads).": "",
  "In paged mode the previous / next page (`pageKeys`; on the first and last page, a screen); in a virtual list a screen up or down.": "",
  "Its buttons one by one: the page sizes, first, previous, the pages, next, last; compact, the page number box (Enter goes there) and the page size list.": "",
  "Sort; add the column to the sort.": "",
  "The column menu; there “Move” and “Width” work with Left and Right, Enter keeps, Escape takes back.": "",
  "Edit the cell; typing starts with that character (a lookup cell opens its list and searches it).": "",
  "Toggle a check box column; empty the cell; edit from empty.": "",
  "In an editor: close it without the value (a new row goes). On a row: take its edits back.": "",
  "The row’s menu: its actions (the selection’s common ones inside a selection of several rows) and what `onContextMenuPreparing` adds; Escape goes back to the cell.": "",
  "The keys that edit and empty a cell are the `editKeys` and `clearKeys` settings; `onKeyHandling` takes any key before the grid does.": "",
  "The next / previous editable cell, row by row; at the end of a new row the next new row opens.": "",
  "Keep the value and go to the row above or below.": "",
  "Move between its buttons; Enter or Space presses one; Alt + Down opens the “more” menu.": "",
  "Select or deselect the row; Space alone where it does not edit (the check box column, a cell that cannot be edited).": "",
  "Extend the selection from the anchor; add or take out one row.": "",
  "Select every row of the filter.": "",
  "Copy the selected rows (multiple selection), else the active cell: tab-separated text and an HTML table.": "",
  "Paste tab-separated text into the editable cells from the active one, rightwards and downwards.": "",
  "Into the cell’s value box; Escape or Enter back to the cell; Tab to the next value box; Delete clears the cell.": "",
  "The condition menu (for a yes/no column, its list).": "",
  "The column menu; without one, the header filter.": "",
  "Move between its items (the toolbar is one Tab stop before the rows); in the search box the arrows stay in its text.": "",
  "Empty the box (the rows come back at once); search without waiting for the pause.": "",
  "Open or close the group.": "",
  "The footer is a row the arrows reach like a group row; the keys that edit or select do nothing there.": "",
  "The row of totals (`totalSummaryTabStop`); Shift + Tab goes back to the active cell. Ctrl + End goes to the last row, as before.": "",
  "Open the group, then go to its first row; close it, then go to the group it is in.": "",
  "Turn the order of the groups; ungroup; move the chip. Left and Right go from chip to chip like any toolbar item.": "",
  "The APG data grid: `role=\"grid\"`, rows and cells with `aria-rowindex` and `aria-colindex`; `aria-rowcount` is the real total, also in a virtual list.": "",
  "Drawn rows are reused while scrolling and stay where they are in the page; the row group lists them in row order with `aria-owns`, so a screen reader reads them top to bottom.": "",
  "Only the active cell is in the Tab order; focus never falls to the page: the focused row stays while it scrolls away.": "",
  "`aria-sort` on the first sorted header.": "",
  "A cell with a message has `aria-invalid` and is described by it while it is active; the status cell names the row’s state, not only with a color.": "",
  "Sorting, moving, saving, errors, copying, pasting and exports are announced through a polite live region.": "",
  "`aria-busy` while the first rows load and while a row is saved in `wait` mode; on a lookup cell while its text loads, and on a cell while its `setCellValue` runs.": "",
  "A key the lookup source does not have is not shown only by its color: it is underlined and its hint (“Not found in the list”) shows on hover and focus.": "",
  "Real buttons with the action’s text as their name (also when only the icon shows, with the text as a tooltip); one of them is in the cell’s roving focus; the “more” button has `aria-haspopup=\"menu\"` and is named “More actions for row N”. In the toolbar and the bottom bar a button that acts on several rows is named with the count (“Approve, 3 rows”) and described by what the bar acts on (“Actions for 3 selected rows”), said politely when that changes; nothing there moves focus by itself.": "",
  "`aria-multiselectable` on the grid, `aria-selected` on every row while selection is on; the check boxes are `role=\"checkbox\"` with `aria-checked` (`mixed` in the header).": "",
  "The filter row is a row of the grid (its fields are named after the column); the condition button names the condition; the header filter is a `dialog` with a listbox.": "",
  "The kit’s `Toolbar` (`role=\"toolbar\"`, named after the grid): one Tab stop with arrow keys between its items; a button that shows only its icon is named by its text, which is also its tooltip and its line in the “more” menu.": "",
  "The box is a search field named “Search in the grid”; the number of records found is announced politely; what was found is marked with `<mark>`, which reads as the same text.": "",
  "Rows of the grid with `aria-expanded` and `aria-level`; their one cell spans the columns (`aria-colspan`), reads “Column: value (count)” and is a cell the arrows reach. Grouping, ungrouping and moving a chip are announced.": "",
  "The row of totals is a row of the grid after the rows (`aria-rowindex`, counted in `aria-rowcount`) in a row group named “Totals”; each cell is named by what its items say about their columns (“Sum of Amount: 1,234”), also when it shows only “Sum: 1,234”. Group footers are rows with `aria-level`; items under their columns in a group row are cells of that row. `aria-busy` while a server works the totals out.": "",
  "A `group` named “Grouping” in the toolbar; each chip is a button named after its column and the order of its groups, described by the keys it takes. Every drag has a keyboard way: the column menu and the chips’ keys.": "",
  "Every text the grid writes — the toolbar, the search box, the bar, the pager, the column menu, the row states, the action buttons, the filter conditions, the summary texts (`gridSummarySum`, `gridSummarySumOtherColumn`, … `gridSummaryCount`, `gridSummarySeparator`, `gridTotalSummary`), the announcements — comes from `uiLocale.strings` (the `grid…` keys), or from the grid's own `texts`. Numbers and dates follow `locale`.": "",
  "The grid. `data-striped`, `data-header-buttons`, `data-mode`.": "",
  "The scrolling area with `role=\"grid\"`, the sticky header, the rows.": "",
  "A row: `data-active`, `data-selected`, `data-status`, `data-odd`, `data-loading`.": "",
  "The actions cell and its buttons (kit button classes, `data-action`).": "",
  "The actions in the toolbar and the bottom bar (kit buttons, `data-action`), their “Actions” menu button, the bottom bar’s toolbar of them, and the hidden text that says what they act on.": "",
  "The selection column and its check box (`aria-checked`).": "",
  "The filter row, its cells, the condition button (`data-set`).": "",
  "The header filter button (`data-active`) and its window.": "",
  "A cell (`data-changed`, `aria-invalid`; a lookup cell `data-lookup=\"loading\"` with `aria-busy`, or `\"missing\"`), a header (`data-sort`, `data-sortable`).": "",
  "The editor of the active cell; its field carries `data-in-cell` and is drawn without a frame.": "",
  "Master-detail: the expand column's cells and their arrow (`aria-expanded`), a row's details and their one cell (`data-fixed` with a `height` of their own); a row with open details carries `data-expanded`.": "",
  "The edit form: the row in place of the edited row and its one cell, the form, a column’s field (`data-field`), the row’s message, Save and Cancel; `__popup` is the window of `editMode: 'popup'`.": "",
  "The toolbar above the rows (the kit’s `.mx-toolbar`) and the gap between its `before` and `after` items.": "",
  "The toolbar’s own items: “New row”, “Save changes”, “Discard”, “Export” (busy while it runs), the column list, the search box.": "",
  "Text the search found, a `<mark>` in the cell.": "",
  "A group row (`data-expanded`, `--_level`), its cell, its arrow and its count.": "",
  "The sticky row group under the rows and its row of totals (`data-state=\"loading\"` while a server works them out).": "",
  "A cell holding summary items (row of totals, group footer, an aligned item of a group row) and each item in it, with the item’s `cssClass`.": "",
  "A group footer (`--_level`); the summary text after a group row’s count.": "",
  "The group panel (`data-drop` while a header can drop there, `data-locked` without dragging), its chips (`data-dir`, `data-dragging`) and its empty text.": "",
  "The bar under the rows and its pager (a `nav`, `data-look=\"full\"` or `\"compact\"`).": "",
  "The pager’s parts: the page size buttons (`aria-pressed`) and their drop-down (compact), the text, the page buttons (`aria-current=\"page\"`), and the page number box (compact).": "",
  "The header filter’s tree of date parts or ranges (the kit’s `TreeView`) and its “Select all” check box.": "",
  "Units: the grid, a row (`header`, `band`, `filter`, `total`, `body`, `group`, `group-footer`, `selected`, drag and drop states), the selection's frame and mark, a cell and a header in their states, the marks over a cell.": "",
  "Units: every other piece, in its states.": "",
  "Sizes the layout counts with.": "",
  "The tints over a row (and its cells): under the pointer, every other row, the keys' row, a new row.": "",
  "Selecting by dragging: the cell ranges' fill, frame and anchor cell; the frame around the rows a drag selects.": "",
  "The edge of the pinned columns, the line under what the search found, the status symbols.": "",
  "The column definitions, in their first order, and bands over them (`{ title, columns }`). See Columns below and [Band headers](/datagrid/bands#bands).": "",
  "`GridAdaptiveDetail`, each field a `Bind`": "",
  "The row’s adaptive detail while columns hide to fit the width (`settings.columnHidingEnabled`, `hidingPriority`): `colCount`, `minColWidth`, `labelMode`, `editors`, `expandOnEdit`, `columnWidth`, `toggleKeys`. Live through `grid.adaptiveDetail`. See [Adaptive columns](/datagrid/bands#adaptive).": "",
  "A row’s adaptive detail lays out its form (`e.formOptions`); it is about to open or close (`e.cancel`), and did.": "",
  "Rows in memory, plain or reactive: the grid reads them as they are and gives the same objects back in events, templates and getters. It puts them in a `DataSource` over an `ArrayAdapter`; a new array (a function that returns one is followed) loads again, a change in place (`push`, `splice`, a field) shows after `refresh()`, `repaint()` or `repaintRows(keys)`. Saved edits, new rows and deletions go into the array.": "",
  "Rows of the data layer, from any adapter. Loading by `blocks` makes a virtual list that asks only where it looks; by `page` a paged grid. Wins over `rows`.": "",
  "The identity of `rows`. A data source uses its adapter’s key.": "",
  "One long list, pages with a pager, or parts that load as the list nears its end (see [Scrolling](/datagrid/scrolling#modes)). A source that loads by page is always paged.": "",
  "Infinite mode: before the next part of the rows loads (`{ skip, take }`, `e.cancel` keeps the rows as they are), and when it came (`{ skip, count, ended }`).": "",
  "Rows per page for rows in memory (0: every row on one page); a source that loads pages or blocks uses its own. The pager’s page sizes (`pageSizeSelector`) and `pageSize(n)` change it; the size the user chose is kept with the layout.": "",
  "Before and after the rows per page change: `{ pageSize, previous }` (0: all); `e.cancel = true` keeps them.": "",
  "When changes are sent: see [Save modes](/datagrid/editing#editing). Changing it starts again with the data (unsaved changes go).": "",
  "bottom": "",
  "Where new rows open and what they start with.": "",
  "Checks a whole row before it is saved: a message per field, or one for the row. `row` is the row itself; `values` holds the values entered and not saved yet, `getValue(field)` the value a field is saved with (the entered one, else the row’s).": "",
  "`GridEditForm` / `GridEditPopup`, each field a `Bind`": "",
  "The edit form of `editMode` `'form'` and `'popup'` (items, columns, labels) and its window (title, size, buttons). Live through `grid.form` and `grid.popup`. See [Edit forms and popups](/datagrid/forms#forms).": "",
  "The feature switches below, each a value or a function.": "",
  "The first sort order; a saved layout (columns, sort and `group`).": "",
  "After the user resized, moved, hid, pinned or sorted.": "",
  "Keeps the layout, the filters and the search text in the browser’s `localStorage` under this name; a grid made again with it gets them back.": "",
  "Where `layoutKey` keeps them: `sessionStorage`, or a store of your own.": "",
  "Every event of the [Events table](/datagrid/layout#events), by its name (`onCellClick`, `onRowUpdating` …); `grid.onCellClick(fn)` listens the same way.": "",
  "`uiLocale` “Data grid”": "",
  "The accessible name. The same as `text`.": "",
  "— / page language": "",
  "Texts of this grid only; the locale of numbers, dates and sorting.": "",
  "from CSS": "",
  "A fixed row height; by default the density decides.": "",
  "The buttons of each row: actions, or the names of the ready ones (`edit`, `remove`, `restore`, `save`, `cancel`). A function is asked per row, again when the row’s state changes (edited, saved, deleted) and on `refreshActions()` or `repaintRows(keys)`.": "",
  "Keys of the selected rows (a function is followed); told after every change of the selection (`e.byDrag` while rows are selected by dragging).": "",
  "The cell ranges (`settings.cellSelection`; a function is followed); asked before a change (`e.cancel`) and told after it (`e.byDrag` while one is drawn). See [Selecting by dragging](/datagrid/drag-select#cells).": "",
  "The first filters, by field: `{ city: { op: '=', value: 'Ankara' }, status: { values: ['Draft'] } }`.": "",
  "The filter value the filter panel shows and the builder edits (with `filterSyncEnabled`, the filter row's and header filters' too) and whether it applies; functions are followed, the user's changes come in `onFilterChanged`. See [Filter panel and builder](/datagrid/filtering#filter-panel).": "",
  "function, objects": "",
  "The panel's text; the builder's props (any of `FilterBuilder` but `value` and `fields`); its window (`title`, `width`, `height`, …).": "",
  "The builder's window opens and closes; the `…ing` ones cancel (`e.apply` says whether OK was pressed).": "",
  "The search panel’s text (a function is followed); told when it changes, typed or set programmatically (`{ text }`). The two together bind it both ways.": "",
  "the items whose features are on": "",
  "The bar above the rows: which items, in which order and place; `visible` left out shows it while it has an item.": "",
  "`{ formats?, allowExportSelectedData?, texts? }`, each a `Bind`": "",
  "What the toolbar’s export button (`exportButton`) offers: a command per format (`'xlsx'`, `'csv'`, any of your own), and “Export selected rows” for each with `allowExportSelectedData`; one command is a plain button, more a menu. `texts`: `exportTo`, `exportAll`, `exportSelectedRows` (`{format}` is the format’s name), `formats` (names by code). Live through `grid.export`.": "",
  "Before and after a group or a row's details open: `{ kind, key, row }` — `kind: 'group'` with the values of the groups from the top level down, or `kind: 'detail'` with the row's key and the row; `e.cancel = true` keeps it closed.": "",
  "Before and after a group or a row's details close; `e.cancel = true` keeps it open.": "",
  "`GridMasterDetail<T>`, each field a `Bind`": "",
  "Details under the rows: the expand column (`enabled`), what they hold (`template`), `autoExpandAll`, `canExpand`, `keepDetails`, `keepAcrossPages`, `keepLimit`, `height`, `estimatedHeight`, `columnWidth`, `toggleKeys`, `arrowKeys`. Live through `grid.masterDetail`. See [Master-detail](/datagrid/master-detail#master-detail).": "",
  "Before and after the grouping changes, by the user or programmatically: `{ group, previous, byUser }`; `e.cancel = true` keeps it.": "",
  "A header or a chip dropped to change the grouping: `{ field, from, to, index }`; `e.cancel = true` cancels the drop.": "",
  "Content of your own in the group rows of columns without a `groupCell`.": "",
  "The summaries: `totalItems` in the row under the rows, `groupItems` in group rows and footers, and how they are worked out. See [Summaries](/datagrid/grouping#summaries).": "",
  "The summary values were worked out again: `{ total, editing }`.": "",
  "The values of a header filter from a server that cannot group: `{ column, search, filter, skip, take, signal }`.": "",
  "An editor was made, in a cell or the edit form; a row is checked before it is saved (add messages, or `isValid = false`). See [Events and methods](/datagrid/forms#form-api).": "",
  "Before a cell editor is made: `{ field, row, values, getValue, isNew, options, cancel }` (`row` is the row itself, `values` what was entered in it, `getValue(field)` the entered value else the row’s). Change `e.options`, the editor’s props (`enabled = false` disables it), or set `e.cancel`.": "",
  "`grid.settings.striped = true`, or a function that is followed.": "",
  "One column’s own switches; `undefined` follows `settings` again.": "",
  "The `DataSource` the rows come from and the `ChangeTracker` of their unsaved changes: listen to them like any other.": "",
  "Rows, the first load running, pages (as `totalCount()` and the standard grid’s `pageCount()`).": "",
  "Assign to change them.": "",
  "Unsaved changes (`{ added, updated, removed, count }`: `added` and `updated` as `{ row, changed }`, the row itself and the values entered apart; `removed` the rows) and rows with errors.": "",
  "The row and the field of the active cell.": "",
  "The ready actions: `edit`, `remove`, `restore`, `save`, `cancel`.": "",
  "The rows the toolbar’s and the bottom bar’s actions act on, and the actions they show: see [Row actions](/datagrid/editing#actions).": "",
  "The selection as a state (`{ all, keys, except, filter }`) and how many rows it holds.": "",
  "read/write, read-only": "",
  "Keys and rows of the selected rows that are known (loaded); assign keys to select them.": "",
  "read/write, read-only; reactive": "",
  "The cell ranges by row key and field (assign to set them); the count, sum, average, smallest and largest of their cells.": "",
  "The selection as a filter of the data layer, for work on the server.": "",
  "The filters by field; the whole filter the rows are loaded with (the search included).": "",
  "read/write, read/write, read-only; reactive": "",
  "The filter value (assigning shares its conditions out to the filter row and header filters with sync), whether it applies, and the panel's text.": "",
  "`grid.filterBuilder.maxGroupLevel = 1`, `grid.filterBuilderPopup.width = '50rem'`; `filterBuilderInstance` is the open builder.": "",
  "The search text; assigning searches at once, a function is followed.": "",
  "The grouped columns in order with the order of their groups (`[{ field, dir }]`); assign to group, `[]` ungroups.": "",
  "The summaries as they read now; assign a new one, or a function that is followed. The items are kept as given: after a change in place call `refreshSummary()`.": "",
  "`'loading'` while a server works out the totals (or every row loads for them), `'error'` when that failed, else `'ready'`.": "",
  "Subscribe with `grid.onRowExpanded((e) => …)`; the same as the props.": "",
  "`grid.form.colCount = 3`, `grid.popup.title = 'Order'`; a function is followed.": "",
  "read/write, live; read-only, reactive": "",
  "`grid.adaptiveDetail.colCount = 1`; the columns the width hides now.": "",
  "`grid.toolbar.items = ['searchPanel', { text: 'Refresh', click }]`, `grid.toolbar.visible = false`; a function is followed. The items are kept as given (`grid.toolbar.items` is your array): after a change in place call `repaint()`.": "",
  "`grid.export.formats = ['xlsx', 'csv']`, `grid.export.allowExportSelectedData = true`; a function is followed.": "",
  "Subscribe with `grid.onSearchTextChanged((e) => …)`; the same as the prop.": "",
  "Subscribe with `grid.onSelectionChanged((e) => …)`.": "",
  "Subscribe with `grid.onEditorPreparing((e) => …)`; the same as the prop.": "",
  "`grid.onRowUpdating((e) => …)` returns a handle; `dispose()` stops listening.": "",
  "`'loading' | 'ready' | 'error'`; the error of the last load; blocks that failed after the first answer.": "",
  "The cell whose editor is open: `{ rowIndex, field, row }`, or `null`.": "",
  "A row is being saved and the grid waits (`wait` mode); an export is running.": "",
  "The active row by index or key; assigning moves there (a key: when its row is loaded).": "",
  "Opens a new row as the “New row” button does; `false` when the row being edited cannot be left.": "",
  "Deletes a row (default: the active one) as the save mode says; takes a batch deletion back.": "",
  "Deletes several rows in one save (one request when the adapter saves in batches), asking once with `confirmDelete`; `false` when a row failed or the user said no.": "",
  "Sends every unsaved change; drops them all.": "",
  "Moves to the next row that failed or has a message.": "",
  "Runs an action on rows (default: the rows the bars act on) as a press does; stops the one working on several rows.": "",
  "Loads again keeping the position (the lookup texts too) and reads everything that shows your data again, the summaries too; loads what failed again. Your data may be plain or reactive; the component reads it as it is. After changing it in place, call `refresh()`.": "",
  "Forgets the texts of the lookup columns and asks for the ones on the screen again.": "",
  "Brings a row into view (in paged mode: its page).": "",
  "Fits the columns; back to the definitions; focuses the active cell.": "",
  "One row in or out of the selection.": "",
  "Every row of the filter, loaded or not; none.": "",
  "Takes every filter away, the filter value too, and the search text.": "",
  "The filter panel's builder window and its Clear, programmatically.": "",
  "Searches for a text at once, as the search panel does; `''` stops searching.": "",
  "Opens the column list, under the toolbar’s column button when it shows.": "",
  "Opens or closes every group of a level (0 is the top level), or of every level.": "",
  "One group by its key, the values from the top level down (`['Ankara', 'Draft']`): whether it opened or closed, and whether it is open.": "",
  "A row's details by the row's key (`masterDetail`): whether they opened or closed (the row events come and can cancel), and whether they are open.": "",
  "Every row's details open or close at once, without row events.": "",
  "A row's adaptive detail by the row's key: whether it opened (the one open closes first) or closed, and whether it is open.": "",
  "Takes every grouping away.": "",
  "Groups by a column at a place among the grouped ones (a grouped one moves); takes one out; sets the order of its groups.": "",
  "What Ctrl+C and Ctrl+V do: copies the cell ranges, the selected rows or the active cell (returns the text); pastes tab-separated text from the active cell or the last range’s first cell, one value into every cell of the ranges (returns the cells written).": "",
  "A range from cell to cell (`{ key or rowIndex, field }`), alone or after the others; none; the selected cells of the loaded rows with their values.": "",
  "The rows of the filter in the sort order, by field, with the visible exportable columns: shown text or `raw` values; a server’s rows in parts through the data source. Group footers and the totals come as objects of the same fields (`summaries: false` leaves them out).": "",
  "The same as a CSV file a spreadsheet opens: byte order mark, the locale’s separator, titles first, a line per group while grouped, group footers after their rows and the totals last. Options: `values`, `selected`, `fileName`, `download`, `separator`, `headers`, `groups`, `summaries`, `bom`, `escapeFormulas`, `pageSize`, `onProgress`, `signal`.": "",
  "What a command of the export button does: `csv` runs `exportCsv`; another format raises `onExporting` with that `format` (and `selectedRowsOnly` from `options.selected`), where the app writes the file.": "",
  "The rows of an export as a sheet of typed cells (header, group rows, data rows, group footers, totals) handed to `write`: what `exportDataGrid` writes, and what a writer of your own (PDF…) takes. Loads like `exportRows`, with the load panel; no `onExporting`, then `onExported`.": "",
  "Stops the export the load panel shows; its promise rejects with an `AbortError`.": "",
  "A value of the totals by the item’s `name`, its place in `totalItems`, its type, its column or `type_column` (`'sum_amount'`). Reactive.": "",
  "A value of a group’s summary, the group by its key (as `expandGroup`), the item as above. Reactive.": "",
  "The rows drawn now: `{ rowIndex, rowType, row, key, groupKey?, element }`.": "",
  "The element of a drawn row or cell.": "",
  "A row’s key by its index, and the index of a loaded row by its key (-1 when it is not loaded).": "",
  "The row with this key: loaded, found before, or asked of the data source.": "",
  "The value a cell shows; with `value`, writes it as the user would (checked, and saved as the save mode says).": "",
  "Goes to the row with this key (its page in paged mode) and makes it the active row.": "",
  "Moves the active cell as the arrows do; opens a cell’s editor, or the first one of a row (in the form modes its form); keeps the open editor’s value and closes it.": "",
  "`editRow` for the row with this key, while it is loaded.": "",
  "Saves or gives up what is being edited, as Save and Cancel do: the edit form, else the row being edited; in batch mode every unsaved change.": "",
  "Changes programmatically in between lay the rows out once, at the last `endUpdate()`.": "",
  "Draws again, without loading, what shows your data: the rows, their details and adaptive detail, the group rows and footers, the totals, the toolbar and the actions (after a row, an option or what a template or `onRowPrepared` reads was changed in place).": "",
  "Draws again only the rows with these keys, with their actions and details: after you changed those rows in place.": "",
  "Reads the summary items again and works the values out again: after an item, the items or the rows’ values were changed in place.": "",
  "Asks every row and both bars for their actions again: after what the `actions` function or an action’s `visible`, `disabled` or `text` reads was changed in place.": "",
  "Reads or writes a column’s `width`, `visible` (`hidden`), `flex`, `sticky`, `visibleIndex`, `sortOrder`, `sortIndex`, `groupIndex`, `filterValues`, `filterType`, a feature switch or any field of its definition (`title`, `format`, `lookup`, `cell`, `type` …: the column is drawn again, its layout, sort and filter kept); without a name, all of them; an object sets several. Each change is told through `onOptionChanged` with the column’s `field`.": "",
  "A column at run time, at a place among the data columns (default: last; what the kept layout says of it applies), or taken out with its sort, grouping and filter. The layout and the kept layout follow; `onOptionChanged` tells `name: 'columns'` with the fields before and after.": "",
  "The data columns, the hidden ones too; the definitions of those shown now, in display order.": "",
  "The page shown (with `n`: go there, as `page`; infinite: the last part shown, with `n` the parts up to it load); the rows per page, 0 for all (with `n`: as the pager’s page sizes, back to the first page, `onPageSizeChanging` first); the rows of every page (infinite: −1 until known).": "",
  "Infinite mode: loads the next part (`onMoreRowsLoading` first); a part is loading; every row shows.": "",
  "The whole filter of the rows: the source’s own, the filter row, the header filters and the search.": "",
  "What the user set up — columns, sort, grouping, filters, search text, page and page size, selected keys, active row — and putting it back.": "",
  "The rows and their saving are the data layer's: `grid.dataSource` and `grid.changeTracker` are a `DataSource` and a `ChangeTracker` of `@motifx-community/data`, with their own events (`onChanged`). `changeTracker.removeRows(rows)` and `removeKeys(keys)` delete several rows in one save, as `deleteRows` does.": ""
}
